.Sh CAVEATS
A USB device's digitizer usages are not mapped, so a touchscreen or pen
that reports through them has no node, and no more than eight
human-interface interfaces of a device are read.
The touchpad drivers are Synaptics', ALPS's and Elantech's alone: another
touchpad, or an ALPS pad of version 9, is driven as the PS/2 mouse it also
is, and a Synaptics or Elantech pad that offers its SMBus bus is driven
over PS/2.
Of Linux's machine quirks for Synaptics pads only the Toshiba rate of 40
is taken: the Cr-48's profile sensor is read as any pad with the advanced
gesture mode.
The serio port has none of Linux's psmouse files,
.Pa protocol ,
.Pa rate ,
.Pa resolution ,
.Pa resetafter
and
.Pa resync_time ,
and an Elantech pad none of its register files,
.Pa reg_07
to
.Pa reg_26 ,
.Pa debug ,
.Pa paritycheck
and
.Pa crc_enabled .
